            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 8,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Please write a commit message.  It doesn't have to be extensive, but should answer \"why?\" this is being done."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 8,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Meis",
                        "email": "christopher.meis@9elements.com",
                        "username": "ChriMarMe"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Can we get a more descriptive filename than \"interface\"?  maybe \"dbus_interface\" ?\n\nTheres's somewhat of a random smattering of things in this.  Maybe it needs broken down into more than one file?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Meis",
                        "email": "christopher.meis@9elements.com",
                        "username": "ChriMarMe"
                    },
                    "message": "All functions transfered here have in common that they operate on a dbus_interface. \n\n- createInterface,\n- addArrayToDbus (which adds an array to an dbus interface, nothing directly to dbus in this function)\n- AddProperty (adds a property to an interface)\n- createDeleteObjectMethod (adds a DeleteObject method to an interface)\n- createAddObjectMehtod (adds an AddObject method to an interface)\n- populateInterfaceFromJson (iterates over json config and uses the functions above)\n\nBecausing naming is hard, it looks unrelated, but these functions are grouped by the fact that they operate on a dbus_interface."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "I agree with Ed that dbus_interface would be more descriptive.  At least something with D-Bus in it.  Without knowing ahead of time, just seeing 'interface' is a bit vague."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
